{"type":"message","id":"de257934","parentId":"edd6d282","timestamp":"2026-03-25T11:10:29.646Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Recommended questions**\nVisible pink urine plus burning makes urinary tract irritation, infection, bleeding from the urinary tract, or another kidney/urologic cause more plausible.\n\n**(3/4)** Have you had any fever or chills, and has the back pain ever become sharp/severe or stayed mainly dull and constant?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_034d3c160a071b9b0169c3c2a3ba4c819198b909a3ec290b98\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":373,"output":72,"cacheRead":27136,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27581,"cost":{"input":0.0009325000000000001,"output":0.00108,"cacheRead":0.006784,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0087965}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774437026453}}
